<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Scroll Use</h1>
<p>Skill
Class: Conjurer (guild level 0), Sorcerer (1), Necromancer (2, up to 80%), Healer (3, up to 80%), Druid (10), Assassin (13, up to 70%), Thief (15, up to 50%)
</p><p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>recite &lt;scroll&gt;
recite &lt;scroll&gt; &lt;target&gt;
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>recite scroll
recite yellow scroll goblin
</pre>
<p>A scroll holds up to three spells. Recite it, and it dissolves as its 
spells are cast at the scroll's own power on the target you name, or on 
yourself if you name none. Scrolls can do almost anything: heal, protect, 
harm a foe, carry you away. To learn what a scroll holds before you 
recite it, identify it (see <a cmd='#'>Help Identify</a>).
</p><p>Reciting takes the scroll use skill: your skill and your brain against 
the scroll's power, so strong scrolls are harder to read. Fail, and 
nothing happens; fail badly, and the scroll crumbles to dust. You must 
carry the scroll, and you can't read it while blind. You can recite while 
resting.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Potions</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Wands</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Identify</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Spells</a>
</pre>




</div>